{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789391921,"nonce":"PyOwGWqQb4VZDvP3bSNT1gwq/PE=","message":"What the polling costs on a kernel, after 8f53003 and 22fa7d3:\nbench_binary_trees.py depth 16 runs at 263 to 285 ms against ZynML's\n212 for the same program with a hand-written release. Node.check may\nraise only on `self.right` being None, so every recursive call is\nfollowed by a load of py$exc, a compare and a branch (two per node),\nand `self.right` is checked again after the first call because a\ncall may have stored to it. That is the whole remaining gap: build is\nat parity. Removing it needs the exception to leave the callee some\nother way than by a global the caller polls; a second return value\nwould move the poll from memory to a register but not remove it.","files":null}]}